// web::fixture — what FastAPI actually answered.
//
// 107 requests were sent through Starlette's test client to a FastAPI
// 0.141 application (Pydantic 2.13, Starlette 1.6, CPython 3.14, from
// `shallowflaws`'s own virtualenv) on 2026-09-19, and every status, `Allow`,
// `Location`, and body was recorded. The application is the one
// `web::demo` reimplements: a registration endpoint shaped like the
// backend's `JobApplicantRegistrationRequest`, a search with validated
// query parameters, and routes with path parameters. `web::demo`'s specs
// replay every request and compare the bytes.
//
// The one edit: `Location` values had Starlette's `http://testserver`
// prefix removed, because `web::route` redirects to a path (see its
// header). `examples/web_oracle.py` captured it and `examples/web_fixture.py`
// wrote this file.
//
// Generated; do not edit by hand.

